scenario:
We're building a simple chat room on Laravel with laravel-echo-server (socket.io), Redis as the queue/broadcast backend, Laravel Echo and Vue. A message typed into an input is POSTed to /chat. The route fires a MessageSent event that implements ShouldBroadcast on the public channel 'test-chat-channel'.

Observed behaviour: the first message produces one console log of the event. The second message produces two, the third produces three, and the count keeps growing with every send. Everything also feels sluggish.

Checks so far:
- laravel-echo-server shows the client joining the channel only once.
- The queue worker processes exactly one broadcast job per message.

Relevant front-end code:
```
methods: {
  sendMessage: function () {
    this.$http.post('/chat', {message: this.message}).then((response) => {
      window.Echo.channel('test-chat-channel')
        .listen('MessageSent', (event) => { console.log(event.message); });
    }, (response) => {});
    this.message = '';
  }
}
```

Why does a single broadcast show up more times with each message sent?

What is the most likely root cause, and how would you fix it?
